// lobe into bay. Scattered through them are the stomata: each a pair of
// kidney-shaped guard cells flanking a central pore, packed with chloroplasts.
// The stomata WORK -- guard cells swell and slacken with turgor so their pores
// open and close, each on its own rhythm plus a slow global light drive, and the
// chloroplasts stream inside; the whole peel drifts gently under the objective.
// Everything runs on incommensurate rates so it never re-phases. Offered as a
